post.description:
## Webhook Ingress

Hit this endpoint with any data that you want to use in the Evari system. This Endpoint supports any body, and any method.

To persist the events getting fired at the webhook on a specific subject/topic, a configuration needs to be created with a trigger like the below. The top 3 conditions are a result of the metadata getting added to the event, the final condition is specific to the data being received by the webhook to allow us to determine the origin (we can also do this with the authentication mechanism).

``` json
"triggers": [
            {
                "condition": {
                    "input": [
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:topic",
                                "WEB_HOOK_"
                            ],
                            "operator": "stringContains"
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:type",
                                "submit-event"
                            ],
                            "operator": "="
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:subject",
                                "$COLLATION/SUBMIT_EVENT"
                            ],
                            "operator": "="
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:body.sg_message_id",
                                null
                            ],
                            "operator": "!="
                        }
                    ],
                    "operator": "and"
                },
                "outcome": true
            }
        ]

 ```

A base configuration of the webhook will look like the below. The function of this is to put the data on a stream with a specific subject and topic specified in the configuration for persistence. This isn't necessary though, as all events will be persisted in collations on this PK and can be used directly `$COLLATION/SUBMIT_EVENT", "topic": "WEB_HOOK_{{guid}}`

``` json
{
    "command": "upsert-configuration",
    "subject": "$COLLATION/DRAFT/CONFIG",
    "topic": "SENDGRID_WEBHOOK",
    "body": {
        "fsm": {
            "state": [
                {
                    "conditions": {
                        "all": [
                            {
                                "referingValue": [
                                    "",
                                    null,
                                    "undefined",
                                    {}
                                ],
                                "internalKey": "BACKBONE",
                                "field": "value",
                                "entity": "questions",
                                "operator": "in"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "value": "BACKBONE"
                }
            ]
        },
        "lookup": {
            "trackingCid": "sengGridWebhook/||$.lookup.topic",
            "subject": "$EMAIL"
        },
        "triggers": [
            {
                "condition": {
                    "input": [
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:topic",
                                "WEB_HOOK_"
                            ],
                            "operator": "stringContains"
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:type",
                                "submit-event"
                            ],
                            "operator": "="
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:subject",
                                "$COLLATION/SUBMIT_EVENT"
                            ],
                            "operator": "="
                        },
                        {
                            "input": [
                                "@fact:body.sg_message_id",
                                null
                            ],
                            "operator": "!="
                        }
                    ],
                    "operator": "and"
                },
                "outcome": true
            }
        ],
        "body": [
            {
                "dataSourceConfiguration": {
                    "options": {
                        "flatMap": false,
                        "useJPath": true,
                        "responseMap": {
                            "topic": "$.lookup.sg_message_id",
                            "body": "$.lookup.trigger_event.body",
                            "type": "$.lookup.event",
                            "subject": "$.lookup.subject"
                        },
                        "backoffMS": 1000,
                        "timeout": 20000,
                        "attempts": 3
                    }
                },
                "dataType": "BACKBONE",
                "internalKey": "BACKBONE"
            }
        ],
        "cid": "$.lookup.topic"
    }
}

 ```

The data in the body can be anything. If it is a single object it will process it as one event. If it is an array like in the example, it will split the objects and process them each as one event into the application.

